[h1]Project Vigilance: Overland Incursions & Geoscape Strategy[/h1]
[b]Replaces instantaneous map-edge teleportation with physical overland transit, dynamic staging, early-warning radar networks, interferometry, orbital logistics, listening posts, and tactical ground interception.[/b]
No high-tech requirements. Zero prerequisites. Safe to add mid-save.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Key Features[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Campaign Creation Wizard & Mutability (New in v0.4):[/b] Dedicated setup page between Storyteller and World settings with 4 presets: [i]Classic Fog of War[/i] (recommended default), [i]Planetary Surveillance[/i], [i]Hardcore Vigilance[/i], and [i]Omniscient[/i]. Features granular rule customization, cryptographic HMAC-SHA256 audit ledger, and [i]Blind Touchdown[/i] (masks unviable landing sites and hazard warnings under Fog of War).
[*] [b]Planetary Radar Infrastructure & Interferometry (New in v0.4):[/b] Native 3D glowing perimeter rings and hexagonal honeycomb radar meshes projected onto the globe. Adds [i]Lookout Towers[/i] (Neolithic), [i]Radar Domes[/i] (Industrial), [i]Spacer Phased Arrays[/i], and [i]SIGINT Consoles[/i]. Features dynamic power scaling, multi-dish classification stacking (10 to 22 rings), and terrain/mountain masking.
[*] [b]Unmanned Listening Posts & Signal Beacons (New in v0.4):[/b] Deploy solar listening relays and stone/wood signal beacons from travelling caravans via right-click hex interaction. Dismantle for 75% material recovery, or repair stations damaged by hostile raiders.
[*] [b]Two-Stage Early Warning & Concealed Sites (New in v0.4):[/b] Stage 1 outer perimeter warning (pulsing amber contact blip) escalates to Stage 2 optical classification upon crossing sensor horizons. Dynamic camps, quest sites, and bandit outposts remain concealed in the Haze of War until scouted (quest timers pause while hidden).
[*] [b]Simulated Inter-Faction Encounters & Trade Routes (New in v0.4):[/b] Physical NPC trade caravans travel between settlements with genuine cargo rosters. Storyteller caravan meetings physically march across the map. Tile clashes resolve via background algebraic skirmishes, leaving persistent aftermath sites with salvageable loot and survivors.
[*] [b]Drifting Keplerian Orbital Logistics & Satellites (New in v0.4):[/b] Analytical Keplerian flight model with J2 nodal precession creating drifting ground tracks across longitudes. Persistent Orbital Station hubs (Trader's Guild), trade satellites with comms console trade windows, drop pod delivery, and dual-layer surface/orbit rendering.
[*] [b]Real-Time Planetary Transit:[/b] Raids, caravans, and visitors spawn at genuine settlements or wilderness staging camps and march across the globe in real time.
[*] [b]Tactical Ground Interception & Forward Ambush:[/b] Intercept hostiles directly on the global hex grid before they reach your colony. Stalk unaware columns, mount night ambushes on sleeping camps, or hail travellers with predictive pursuit vectoring.
[*] [b]Retreat Lifecycle, Pursuit & Kidnap Recovery:[/b] Defeated enemies physically retreat across the world map with wounds, loot, and captured colonists intact. Track wounded raiders overland, rescue captives before they reach home bases, or assault strongholds to liberate prisoners.
[*] [b]Evacuated Colony Hierarchy & Track Pursuit:[/b] Raiders reaching vacant or abandoned colonies search for tracks to launch hot pursuit after fleeing player caravans, divert toward secondary outposts, or ransack the site and head home.
[*] [b]Night Owl & Schedule-Aware Caravaning:[/b] Caravans respect colonist traits and schedules. Pure Night Owls sleep during the day (11:00–18:00) and march at night without darkness penalties. Mixed squads maintain camp watch for 24/7 vision.
[*] [b]Pack Animal Cargo & Roadside Barter:[/b] Trade stock remains in pack animal inventories across all battle maps without floor-dumping. Barter with friendly travelling merchants directly on the road.
[*] [b]Classic 3-Tier Haze of War:[/b] [i]Shrouded[/i] (unexplored mask), [i]Obscured[/i] (surveyed geography), and [i]Monitored[/i] (live sensory coverage). Approaching forces outside sight lines receive classified X-COM contact IDs.
[*] [b]Dynamic Nighttime & Sleep Simulation:[/b] Detection horizons drop by 50% in darkness. Lookouts collapse to a tight perimeter when colonists sleep. Biological forces camp at night, while Mechanoids and Anomalies march 24/7.
[*] [b]Configurable Settings & Scope Preview:[/b] Fully customizable sight ranges, caravan vision, night penalties, and march speeds in Mod Options, complete with a live CRT radar scope preview.
[*] [b]Custom Visual Assets & Thermal Integrity (New in v0.4.1):[/b] Dedicated faction-tinted sprites for sensory structures, outposts, and orbital satellites, plus startup thermal integrity calibration preventing unrealistic burning of solid metals, all-metal machinery, radar dishes, and heavy steel bridges while preserving wooden bridges, Bioferrite hulls, and battery fire hazards.
[/list]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatibility & Performance[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]DLC Compatibility:[/b] 100% compatible with Base Game, Royalty, Ideology, Biotech, Anomaly, and Odyssey.
[*] [b]Save Games:[/b] Safe to add mid-save. Safe to remove (in-flight world incursions disband cleanly).
[*] [b]Era Agnostic:[/b] Seamless across neolithic, medieval, industrial, and spacer playthroughs.
[*] [b]Performance:[/b] Zero-allocation spatial bitmasks and time-sliced 3D mesh layers guarantee buttery-smooth 60+ FPS with zero TPS impact.
[/list]
[h2]Recommended Load Order[/h2]
[olist]
[*] Harmony
[*] Core
[*] All Official DLCs (optional)
[*] [b]Project Vigilance - Overland Incursions[/b]
[/olist]
